 * command mode supports vim-style visual selection in the focused pane: (v) selects characters,
     (V) selects full rows, and (Ctrl-V) selects a rectangular block. h/j/k/l and arrow keys extend
     the selection, (y) copies the selection, and (Y) copies complete selected rows.
+* when an agent chat is selected, slash-prefixed text like (/status) is sent to that selected agent.
+    Pressing (/) in command mode opens the selected chat with the slash already typed; prompt-mode
+    slash commands route to the selected agent only when an agent chat is selected.
 * (s) open the chate in the same pane (it spplit the left part in 2 3 ecc ecc so can open
     many chat)
 * (t) open the chat in a new window (gt go next window gT prev window)
diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index d6d521c..a3b37f2 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -246,6 +246,11 @@ part of the DTO surface for full-session replacement when an integration needs i
 appends and status changes are not paired with full-session replacement events, so remote frontends
 can update long transcripts without re-receiving the full transcript text.
 
+`WorkLeafController::execute_command_line` treats a slash-prefixed token with no intervening
+whitespace, such as `/status`, as a selected-agent message when a selected session exists. Without a
+selected agent, the same text remains command-surface input and is handled by the command worker or
+reported as an unknown command by terminal adapters.
+
 New UIs should consume `WorkLeafController` and these DTOs. They should not duplicate worker
 spawning, session naming, review lookup, loading bookkeeping, or orchestrator event routing.
 
